          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. What is a balanced chemical equation? Why should chemical equations be balanced?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.143,
            0.3,
            0.892,
            0.321
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. Translate the following statements into chemical equations and then balance them.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.322,
            0.726,
            0.342
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(a) Hydrogen gas combines with nitrogen to form ammonia.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.343,
            0.84,
            0.363
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(b) Hydrogen sulphide gas burns in air to give water and sulpur dioxide.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.364,
            0.894,
            0.4
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(c) Barium chloride reacts with aluminium sulphate to give aluminium chloride and a precipitate of barium sulphate.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.401,
            0.894,
            0.438
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(d) Potassium metal reacts with water to give potassium hydroxide and hydrogen gas.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.143,
            0.439,
            0.551,
            0.459
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6. Balance the following chemical equations.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.46,
            0.531,
            0.482
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(a)",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{HNO_{3}+Ca(OH)_{2}\\rightarrow Ca(NO_{3})_{2}+H_{2}O}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.482,
            0.509,
            0.502
          ],
          "content": [
